1. Install the core tools

Python 3.11 → python.org
PostgreSQL 16 → postgresql.org (when installing, it'll ask you to set a password for the postgres user — write that down, you'll need it in a few minutes)
Git + create a GitHub repo called carebridge-ai
VS Code as your editor

2. Create your folder structure

carebridge-ai/
├── backend/        ← this is yours
├── frontend/        ← your teammates work here
└── README.md

3. Set up your Python virtual environment

bash
cd carebridge-ai/backend
python -m venv venv
venv\Scripts\activate        # Windows


4. Create the database
    4.1
        Create a server in PostgreSQL
        Create a Database named as carebridge

                    (or)
    bash
        psql -U postgres
        CREATE DATABASE carebridge;
    \q

